        "id": 1330845
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-03-18T17:47:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "That\u0027s not the EIP that is the parameter to watchdog_warning though. Errorcode, EIP, CS, and EFLAGS are pushed by the interrupt handler, *then* call pushes the return address (the EIP you were looking at). When we call watchdog_warning, the parameter named \"eip\" comes from the interrupt handler; we\u0027re not talking about the return address.",
      "parentUuid": "c1eb0093_78806689",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 66,
        "startChar": 11,
        "endLine": 66,
        "endChar": 13
